WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.279
Panic and terror gripped everyone in the Foundation
facility…

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:07.779
well, everyone who was still alive, that is.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:12.020
Guards were working tirelessly to fight back
and regain control of the building, but they

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.059
didn’t have enough bullets to suppress the
oncoming horde.

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:21.260
Somehow, a sample of SCP-008 that was being
examined for testing purposes had managed

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.990
to spread to one of the research staff.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.939
Before long, the very same researcher was
now a mindless zombie, a reanimated corpse

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.520
that had managed to bite several other staff
members, spreading the infection.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.780
It didn’t matter that this original carrier
was shot down by security personnel, it had

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.480
already done its damage and passed on SCP-008.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.710
By now, there were too many of them to simply
bonk each one on the head and neutralize it.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.800
The Foundation facility had gone into a full-scale
lockdown, an emergency quarantine to try and

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.489
limit the spread of the deadly virus.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:01.410
Any exit to the outside world was shut, and
would stay sealed tight unless someone from

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.300
the Foundation could do something.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:08.130
But that meant the few surviving members of
staff trapped inside were at the mercy of

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.740
the zombie horde.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.979
Their options were limited; SCP-500 was known
to perfectly cure those infected with SCP-008,

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:22.310
but with all exits locked, it was impossible
to get any of the remaining SCP-500 pills

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.330
on site.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:30.140
Then, one of the surviving researchers, one
Doctor Omel, had an idea; it was an insanely

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.790
risky plan, one that the Foundation would
never sign off on.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:37.710
But desperate times called for desperate measures.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:43.450
Gathering up the remaining security forces
that hadn’t been infected with SCP-008,

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:48.200
along with a research assistant that had managed
to escape the zombies, Doctor Omel and his

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.909
band of survivors headed deeper into the facility.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:56.409
While the external doors were all locked to
prevent the SCP-008 infectees from making

00:01:56.409 --> 00:02:00.990
it out and spreading the virus to the wider
world, the doors inside the facility were

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.119
all still functioning.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:04.649
And it was a good thing, too.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:10.649
Doctor Omel’s plan relied on opening the
doors to two anomalies: SCP-914, the Clockworks,

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:17.920
a machine capable of destroying or refining
anything placed inside it… and SCP-049,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.349
the Plague Doctor.

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:21.380
It was a shot in the dark at best.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:26.230
Omel had observed the Plague Doctor for some
time, and knew that the beak-faced surgeon

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:33.220
was capable of creating zombie-like creatures
known as SCP-049-2, not dissimilar from the

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.620
zombies infected with SCP-008.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:41.290
If anyone could potentially fix this nightmare,
there were few as well versed in anomalous

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.700
medicine as SCP-049.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.670
Taking him to the Clockworks was, however,
an even bigger risk.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:56.599
Normally, SCP-049 killed any he touched, and
turned their deceased bodies into SCP-049-2s,

00:02:56.599 --> 00:03:01.390
hence Doctor Omel calling for a refinement
of the Plague Doctor’s abilities.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:07.090
Placing him in the Input booth of SCP-914
and setting it to ‘Very Fine’, Omel prayed

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:12.200
he’d made the right call; he could hear
the horde of SCP-008 pounding outside the

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.580
locked door…

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:19.130
What emerged from the Clockworks was still
recognizable as SCP-049, retaining his beaked

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:25.290
mask – although the mask itself was actually
flesh and bone, a part of his skull.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.920
His robes now flowed out behind him as a pair
of dark, feathery wings, giving him an even

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.840
more bird-like appearance.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.670
Despite this, SCP-049 had claimed that he’d
never been a bird before.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.680
“Didn’t expect wings, I’ll admit,”
the surviving assistant remarked.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.900
“It’s not so surprising, really,” Doctor
Omel admitted.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.189
“He did lay an egg that one time.”

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:48.989
“What, he did what?!”

00:03:48.989 --> 00:03:53.700
Before an explanation could be given, the
SCP-008 zombies managed to break down the

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.040
door and came flooding into the room.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.530
Omel recoiled in horror as they snarled and
shuffled closer, reaching towards him with

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.079
decrepit fingers.

00:04:02.079 --> 00:04:07.510
Suddenly, SCP-049 swooped into the path of
the encroaching undead with a flap of his

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.510
new wings.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.329
Calmly, he gave a gentle move of his hand,
like lifting something from a shelf.

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:18.070
A bizarre contraption appeared around his
forearm, a gauntlet connected to syringes

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:23.009
that were strapped to each of his fingers,
all filled with various different fluids.

00:04:23.009 --> 00:04:29.250
Doctor Omel was amazed, SCP-049 seemed to
now have the anomalous ability to summon surgical

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.760
equipment from a tiny pocket dimension.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:38.280
It was almost exactly like SCP-076-2, Able,
drew his weapons.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:44.370
Reaching towards the nearest SCP-008 zombie,
still moving with the utmost calm, SCP-049

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.670
stated:
“Now, try to hold still,” he spoke in

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:53.880
a gentle voice, with a bedside manner most
medical doctors would be incapable of.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.960
“This might sting a little.”

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.940
With that, SCP-049 pushed the syringes into
the zombie, the fluids draining from each

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.100
one, then refilling as he withdrew his hand.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:09.820
The SCP-008 instance froze for a moment, almost
like it was confused, before it began to emit

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:14.650
what looked to be steam, as though it had
stepped out of a hot shower.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:19.820
Shaking uncontrollably, the necrosis and tell-tale
signs of infection seemed to disappear, like

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:25.970
being washed away, until all that was left
of the SCP-008 zombie was the infected researcher

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.680
it had been before.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.040
The man was alive and well, much to Doctor
Omel’s astonishment.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:40.509
SCP-049 hadn’t just cured the SCP-008 infection,
he’d actually reversed it, leaving the infectee

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:41.780
alive and well.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:47.620
It took a few hours for SCP-049 to fly around
the facility on his new wings, effortlessly

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:52.660
turning all the SCP-008 zombies back into
their old selves one by one.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.770
By the time he was done, everyone on site
that had previously been exposed to SCP-008

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.650
was cured.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.240
And it didn’t stop there.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:06.419
The Foundation still mandated everyone who
was previously infected to remain in quarantine

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:12.860
whilst they were examined, remanding the now
refined SCP-049 back to his cell, which he

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.470
politely complied with.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:19.580
When the SCP Foundation doctors took a look
at the formerly zombified staff, they were

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.430
amazed at what they found.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:27.160
Each one had all traces of SCP-008 completely
removed from their systems.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.590
Trying to re-expose them to the virus, their
bodies now seemed able to generate anomalous

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:39.340
antibodies that rejected and fought off infection
by SCP-008 in a manner of seconds.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:42.590
The Plague Dcotor had made everyone immune.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:47.870
Upon further testing, examining skin and blood
cells from the former infectees, and performing

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:53.440
full top-to-bottom health checks, the Foundation
doctors learned something else too.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:58.560
Everyone that SCP-049 had cured was even healthier
than they had been before.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.449
One security guard had been a one-pack-a-day
smoker for ten years, but an X-Ray revealed

00:07:03.449 --> 00:07:08.229
any damage to his lungs, mouth, and throat
had all been completely reversed.

00:07:08.229 --> 00:07:13.990
On every possible internal and external level,
the formerly zombified personnel had all been

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.210
returned to pristine health by SCP-049.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:22.139
Eager to witness the full extent of these
new anomalous abilities the Clockworks had

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:27.169
given him, the SCP Foundation struck a deal
with SCP-049.

00:07:27.169 --> 00:07:31.539
If he performed a mission for them, then they
would provide him with the means to have anything

00:07:31.539 --> 00:07:32.539
he wanted.

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:36.710
For a moment, the Plague Doctor pondered their
terms, and then agreed.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.819
“What is it you want in return?”

00:07:38.819 --> 00:07:39.919
Doctor Omel had asked.

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:45.320
“To cure the world, Doctor,” SCP-049 replied
simply.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.640
The Plague Doctor flew as fast as his wings
would carry him to the location the Foundation

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:50.640
had given him.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:55.330
It was an isolated region in Siberia, kept
completely cut off from the rest of the world

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.759
by guards working around the clock.

00:07:57.759 --> 00:08:03.760
Arriving at the edge of the frozen town, SCP-049
was approached by the security commander,

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.930
and given his full directive from the Foundation.

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:10.460
“Your objective, I’m told, is simple:
you enter the restricted area, and neutralize

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.430
anything you come into contact with.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.710
When you’re done, return here and we’ll
report the results to command.”

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:19.130
“Thank you, Commander,” the Plague Doctor
nodded graciously.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.870
“You’ve been most helpful.”

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.210
He didn’t ask what was out there, merely
turned and began walking through the snow

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:28.310
until he could no longer be seen by the eye.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:33.459
Maybe he had already sensed what was out there,
what kind of sickness plagued this place,

00:08:33.459 --> 00:08:37.460
and understood exactly the Foundation were
asking him to do about it.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:41.690
If SCP-049 had any questions, he didn’t
make them known.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:48.420
Instead, he just headed off in search of every
instance of SCP-610 he could find.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.670
There was quiet for an uncomfortably long
while.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:56.050
The personnel standing guard at the edge of
the area watched through the snowfall, ready

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:59.180
if anything started slithering its way towards
them.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.760
The Foundation security all tensed when the
motion sensor picked up movement, accompanied

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:09.510
by the sounds of fighting, and the bizarre,
inhuman noises instances of SCP-610 made.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:15.950
Then, after another long period of unsettling
quiet, somebody spotted a gently glowing light

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.920
making its way through the snow.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:23.610
As it drew closer, the glow of the burning
makeshift torch made it clear the figure holding

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.339
it was SCP-049.

00:09:26.339 --> 00:09:31.510
And as he made his way towards the rendezvous
point, it quickly became apparent he wasn’t

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:32.510
alone.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:36.720
Shivering in the freezing cold and wet from
the snow, covered in scraps of dirty clothing

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.590
and whatever else they could find, was a huddled
mass of people.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:45.529
All of them looked bewildered, following the
light of SCP-049’s torch like a guiding

00:09:45.529 --> 00:09:47.899
beacon towards the edge of the perimeter.

00:09:47.899 --> 00:09:52.490
The Foundation security all stood slack-jawed
in amazement at what happened, while the Plague

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:57.260
Doctor led the people and urged the commander
that they all needed warmer clothing immediately.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:02.670
He’d done it: SCP-049 had cured the Flesh
That Hates.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:06.930
In the coming months, the Foundation soon
found themselves very busy.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:11.720
Everyone who had previously been infected
by SCP-610 needed to be screened and examined,

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:16.690
just to make absolutely sure there was no
chance they could mutate into a fleshy monstrosity

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.690
again.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:22.920
But, just like before with the former SCP-008
zombies, these people were all in perfect

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.530
condition: cured and healthier than they had
ever been.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:32.089
By using his new anomalous surgical skill
and healing power, SCP-049 had returned the

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:35.790
Flesh That Hates’ victims back into human
beings.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:40.730
It was starting to seem like there was no
disease, no infection – anomalous or otherwise

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:43.089
– that he couldn’t cure.

00:10:43.089 --> 00:10:48.240
The Foundation began an effort to rehouse
the former SCP-610 infectees.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:52.600
Given that most of them had spent years as
aggressive anomalous abominations, almost

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:56.880
every one of them had been officially pronounced
dead and couldn’t just go back to their

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.180
old lives.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:03.060
The SCP Foundation gradually reintroduced
them into the world, setting up new identities

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:06.000
and integrating them into new countries.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.550
SCP-049 even personally helped console some
of those that struggled with the adjustment,

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.730
offering to give them therapy to aid in the
process.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:19.220
He was more than just a Plague Doctor, it
seemed, thanks to the Clockworks.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.030
SCP-049’s good work didn’t stop with curing
the Flesh That Hates, either.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:28.170
As promised, the Foundation allowed him to
carry out his newfound purpose.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.410
Whereas before, he was obsessed with eradicating
what he called ‘The Pestilence’, now the

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:37.139
Plague Doctor seemed to be directing all of
his focus to ‘curing the world’ as he

00:11:37.139 --> 00:11:38.139
put it.

00:11:38.139 --> 00:11:41.060
And he started with some of his fellow anomalies.

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:45.790
The Plague Doctor started experimenting with
his new tools, concocting cures and serums

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:51.380
aplenty by pulling whatever he needed from
an endless supply of equipment and ingredients

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.380
at his fingertips.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:57.700
He developed a cure for the condition that
had caused Daniel MacIntyre to become SCP-2800,

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.180
Cactusman.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.860
His skin reverted back to normal, no longer
sporting spines, while the plant-like parts

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.950
of his DNA once again became human.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:11.850
SCP-049 even offered a sympathetic ear to
a lot of Daniel’s troubles, helping therapize

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:15.700
him through a lot of his mental health difficulties.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:21.380
SCP-2102 was also one of SCP-049’s successful
patients.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:25.621
His condition of rapidly over-producing new
skin tissue when injured quickly became a

00:12:25.621 --> 00:12:27.029
thing of the past.

00:12:27.029 --> 00:12:31.760
Then, the Plague Doctor turned his sights
to the wider world, working tirelessly to

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:37.690
create new vaccinations and treatments for
diseases that were once thought to be incurable.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.351
Everything he made and had the Foundation
distribute to those that needed it, was all

00:12:41.351 --> 00:12:44.290
one hundred percent effective.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:49.840
People were healthier and happier than ever,
all thanks to the Plague Doctor.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.649
Until they weren’t…

00:12:51.649 --> 00:12:57.130
In attempting to eradicate disease the world
over, a new strain of illness emerged.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:02.780
SCP-049 took to calling it a ‘New Pestilence’,
and it was nothing short of horrific.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:08.130
It would have been considered anomalous at
one time, but it quickly became so widespread

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.240
that it couldn’t be contained.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:14.070
All the Plague Doctor’s advanced medical
treatments had encouraged this disease to

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:17.230
mutate, to adapt against everything he could
throw at it.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:23.100
It could infect any person, at any time, and
present itself with virtually any symptoms.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:27.440
It resisted drugs, any form of treatment,
and spread rapidly.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:31.240
Eventually, while trying to come up with a
way to protect people from this strain of

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:37.810
super bacteria, this ‘New Pestilence’,
SCP-049 started to fall ill.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:42.650
He had caught it, and even with his refinement,
he was beginning to weaken.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:48.050
The Plague Doctor was dying, and once he was
gone, the whole world would soon follow as

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.190
more and more people caught the sickness.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:55.850
There was only one thing he could do, a way
to leave someone behind to carry on his work.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:01.170
When the Foundation – those that weren’t
yet ill – found SCP-049, he had already

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.170
passed.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:06.360
But alongside his body was something smooth
and pearlescent: an egg.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.589
And inside?

00:14:08.589 --> 00:14:12.090
Maybe a chance for the world to be cured.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:13.600
Want an anomaly of your own?

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.000
Check out www.scpswag.com for high-quality
SCP merch!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:22.250
Now go check out “WHAT IF THE FLESH THAT
HATES WAS PUT INSIDE SCP-914?”

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:27.850
and “SCP-049 - BOILED, SCRAMBLED AND FRIED
- PLAGUE DOCTOR TALE” for more pestilent

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:28.860
entertainment!

